## Design (per `scoreboard_reference_model_strategy`)

- **Predictor-style**: `build_phase` resolves exactly the §6 ConfigDB keys (`KEY_DUT_PINS`, `KEY_CLK_RST`, `KEY_CONF`) with the same `ConfigDB().get(self, "", KEY_...)` call form the existing monitor/driver use, and creates `uvm_tlm_analysis_fifo("hamming_analysis_fifo")` exposing `analysis_export` (env stage connects `agent.monitor_ap` to it).
- **Sample/compare**: `run_phase` loops `await analysis_fifo.get()`; per item it validates geometry (item ↔ `HammingConf` ↔ `HammingParams` must agree → `RuntimeError` on setup bugs), calls `hamming_encode(item.data_in, item.data_width, item.secded)`, masks to `params.code_width`, and compares bit-for-bit. Combinational latency-0, so no pipeline/deskew — the monitor item already pairs `data_in`/`code_out` at the same settle boundary.
- **Error reporting**: any bit difference logs `data_in` (bin+hex), `DATA_WIDTH`, `SECDED`, expected/actual `code_out` (bin+hex), differing bit indices (LSB-first), and a best-effort live-pin snapshot, then raises `AssertionError` — flagging the error immediately and failing the current test, as the plan's `error_reporting` dictates.
- **Reset**: stateless predictor + monitor only publishing genuine drives means nothing can go stale; `reset_checker()` is the documented hook (env/tests stage MUST call it per `tb_reset` phase) that clears per-block counters while preserving the cumulative per-`(DATA_WIDTH, SECDED)` stats.
- **Reporting**: `report_phase` emits a per-block summary plus the cumulative per-configuration summary (checked/passed/mismatches).
- Watchdog deliberately remains owned by the stage-5 coverage/assertions module (same split as the FIFO bench, per CONTRACT §9); no scoreboard-local watchdog.

No transaction/sequencer/driver/sequences/monitor/agent/coverage/assertions/env/tests/tb_top were generated; RTL/spec/plan/reference model were not modified.

