  evidence:
  - 'simulation_result.json: every test used the same SIM_BUILD with no -G/parameter
    overrides and no DATA_WIDTH/SECDED env, so the RTL default elaboration (DATA_WIDTH=4,
    SECDED=0) was active for the whole regression'
  - 'HammingTC3Test/TC5Test/TC7Test logs end at <=20ns with ''monitor: observed and
    published 1 transaction(s)'' and ''HammingScoreboard report: 1 items checked,
    1 passed'' although their sequences (SpecExampleHamming84SECDEDSeq requires SECDED=1;
    ExhaustiveSweepHamming128Seq requires DATA_WIDTH=8; ParameterizedWidthConfigurationsSeq
    requires DATA_WIDTH in {1,11,16}) skipped on the active elaboration'
  - All per-test coverage files (tb/hamming_encoder_coverage_HammingTC*.xml/yml) show
    zero hits on secded_on, width_1, width_8, width_11, width_16, secded_parity_zero,
    secded_parity_one; merged tb/hamming_encoder_coverage.xml reports 41.67% aggregate
    coverage
  - The plan's TC4 exhaustive sweep defined 32 combos (16 data words x SECDED 0/1);
    only the 16 SECDED=0 vectors were ever exercised. TC6/TC8 'both SECDED modes'
    likewise reduced to the active mode only
  - Corner-case sequences MinimumDataWidth, ParityBitCountTransition, SECDEDOrderingShift,
    SECDEDCodewordEvenWeight all log-and-skip under the active elaboration (their
    SECDED parity/ordering and R=2/R=4/R=5 checks never ran)
  likely_cause: 'Inference: the generated tests implement an ''adaptive-skip'' design
    (test.py elaboration_applies + sequences.py _targets): any scenario inapplicable
    to the active elaboration logs and passes without stimulus, and the runner only
    elaborated the RTL default configuration, converting most of the planned parameter
    matrix into silent no-ops that still report pass'
  investigation_targets:
  - 'tb/test.py: elaboration_applies() per test class and report_phase() skip path'
  - 'tb/sequences.py: _targets() log-and-skip guard and per-sequence elaboration guards'
  - 'tb/test_top.py: DATA_WIDTH/SECDED parameter resolution from env/defaults'
  - tb/Makefile and the worker command list in simulation_result.json (no per-config
    elaboration)
  recommended_action: Elaborate and run the DUT for every (DATA_WIDTH, SECDED) member
    of the plan matrix (e.g. -G DATA_WIDTH=8, SECDED=1 per run) and make each scenario's
    test fail or be reported as 'unexercised' when its target elaboration is not active,
    instead of passing via skip; gate the regression on the plan's per-configuration
    coverage bins
