- id: W-PHANTOM-PRIMED-TRANSACTION
  severity: medium
  category: monitor-sampling
  title: Monitor publishes a phantom transaction for the pre-stimulus primed (data_in=0,
    code_out=0) pair, so tests that drove nothing still report '1 item checked, 1
    passed'
  affected_tests:
  - HammingTC1Test
  - HammingTC2Test
  - HammingTC3Test
  - HammingTC4Test
  - HammingTC5Test
  - HammingTC6Test
  - HammingTC7Test
  - HammingTC8Test
  - HammingCornerTest
  - HammingRandomizedTest
  evidence:
  - 'HammingTC3Test log: 1 transaction observed and 1 scoreboard check passed although
    SpecExampleHamming84SECDEDSeq skipped (SECDED=0 active, no drive); same 1-item
    profile in TC5 and TC7'
  - tb/test_top.py primes dut.data_in.setimmediatevalue(0) at time 0 and the combinational
    code_out settles to 0, so pins_driven() is True from the first monitor sample
    with no drive having occurred
  - 'tb/monitor.py run_phase: the first X/Z-free sample is published because prev_pair
    is None and pair != prev_pair; the docstring''s claimed lock ''lands on the settle
    boundary of the first drive'' is not guaranteed when the idle pair is already
    X/Z-free'
  - 'tb/hamming_encoder_coverage_HammingTC3Test.yml etc.: exactly one hit each on
    (zero, secded_off), i.e. coverage of the primed idle pair, not of any driven vector'
  - 'HammingTC4Test: for the 16-vector sweep the monitor published 16 items; the zero
    drive''s settled pair (0,0) is identical to the idle primed pair, so it is absorbed
    into a single (0,0) publication and the zero vector is never independently re-checked
    by the scoreboard'
  - HammingTC1Test (reset window then a single drive of 0) and HammingTC2Test (single
    drive of 0b0101) each drive exactly one vector yet publish 1 and 2 items respectively
    -- the first-publish rule absorbs the idle (0,0) pair whenever an X/Z-free sample
    precedes the first settle, making the item count timing-dependent
  likely_cause: 'Inference: the monitor''s change-pair publishing logic cannot distinguish
    the idle primed input from a genuine drive; with data_in=0 primed before any sequence
    runs, the first sample is treated as a settled transaction'
  investigation_targets:
  - 'tb/monitor.py: run_phase() lock/first-publish logic'
  - 'tb/test_top.py: hamming_tb_top() setimmediatevalue priming'
  - 'tb/dut_helper.py: pins_driven()'
  recommended_action: 'Suppress the initial primed sample: seed prev_pair with the
    first X/Z-free sample without publishing, or publish only after the driver has
    completed its first item (e.g. a ''drives_done'' counter/Q), and have skipped/no-stimulus
    tests report 0 items rather than 1'
  confidence: high
- id: W-COALESCED-PAIR-SCOREBOARD-COUNT
  severity: medium
  category: scoreboard-blindspot
  title: Monitor coalesces back-to-back identical (data_in, code_out) pairs, so the
    scoreboard and coverage never re-check the duplicate-driven vectors (930 of 1000
    randomized vectors scored)
  affected_tests:
  - HammingRandomizedTest
  evidence:
  - 'HammingRandomizedTest log: monitor ''observed and published 930 transaction(s)''
    and scoreboard ''930 items checked, 930 passed'', while tb/test.py RANDOM_VECTORS=1000
    and the sequence drives and self-checks num_vectors=1000'
  - 'tb/monitor.py docstring: ''Two back-to-back transactions that drive the identical
    data word coalesce into one item'''
  - 'Boundary-concentrated generation (boundary_prob=0.25: zero/max/single-bit/near-max)
    makes duplicate data words frequent; tb/hamming_encoder_coverage_HammingRandomizedTest.yml
    shows zero=97, max_value=98, single_bit_set=242 hits within only 930 samples'
  likely_cause: 'Inference: publish-on-pair-change is a set semaphore, not an event
    counter; repeated inputs are deliberately collapsed, so the passive scoreboard/coverage
    subscribers see fewer items than were driven, contradicting the plan''s claim
    that the scoreboard re-checks every driven vector'
  investigation_targets:
  - 'tb/monitor.py: run_phase() changed-pair publish rule'
  - 'tb/scoreboard.py: _num_items_checked accounting'
  - 'tb/sequences.py: HammingRandomizedSequence duplicate generation'
  recommended_action: Attach a per-drive sequence number/drive counter to monitor
    items and check the scoreboard's checked count equals the number of completed
    sequence items; alternatively have the driver emit one item per item_done regardless
    of pair identity and let the sequence feed duplicate-free expected values
  confidence: high
- id: W-COVERAGE-GOALS-NOT-ENFORCED
  severity: medium
  category: coverage-gating
  title: Plan functional-coverage goals are exported but never enforced; tests pass
    with 0% hit on the SECDED/width bins they were planned to cover
  affected_tests:
