    coverage: tb/test.py report_phase only checks _num_mismatches and _num_items_checked'
  - tb/coverage.py report_phase only prints/merges coverage; merged tb/hamming_encoder_coverage.xml
    shows 41.67% with secded_on=0, width_1/8/11/16=0, secded_parity_zero/one=0 while
    all 10 tests still report pass
  - Per-test coverage percentages for passing tests are 22-42% (e.g. HammingTC3Test
    22.22%, HammingCornerTest varied), with no threshold applied
  likely_cause: 'Inference: coverage was implemented as instrumentation plus reporting,
    but the pass criteria were never wired to the coverage database, so the coverage
    goals are decorative and skipped tests contribute 0 relevant hits yet pass'
  investigation_targets:
  - 'tb/coverage.py: report_phase()/coverage_db usage'
  - 'tb/test.py: report_phase() pass criteria'
  recommended_action: Evaluate coverage goals in report_phase for applicable elaborations
    (fail when required bins such as secded_on/secded_parity_* are un-hit, or when
    the plan's cross bins are unreached), and surface per-configuration coverage alongside
    test status
  confidence: high
- id: W-GEOMETRY-NOT-VALIDATED-AGAINST-ELABORATION
  severity: low
  category: configuration-integrity
  title: HammingConf geometry is derived from env/defaults and never cross-verified
    against the actual elaborated DUT port widths, so a misconfigured (or rtl_info-default)
    elaboration would be scored with the wrong geometry
  affected_tests:
  - HammingTC1Test
  - HammingTC2Test
  - HammingTC3Test
  - HammingTC4Test
  - HammingTC5Test
  - HammingTC6Test
  - HammingTC7Test
  - HammingTC8Test
  - HammingCornerTest
  - HammingRandomizedTest
  evidence:
  - tb/test_top.py builds HammingConf from DATA_WIDTH/SECDED env vars (defaults 4/0)
    with no probe of the live DUT port widths; the scoreboard's geometry cross-check
    (tb/scoreboard.py _check_geometry) only compares HammingConf vs HammingParams,
    both derived from the same env value
  - verification_plan.yaml DISC-1 documents that rtl_info.json reports wrong parameter
    defaults (SECDED='1', CODE_WIDTH='1'), so relying on metadata/defaults to agree
    with the RTL is known-fragile
  - In this run defaults coincided with the RTL defaults (no -G/overrides in the command
    lines), so no mismatch occurred, but the environment has no guard that would catch
    a silent divergence
  likely_cause: 'Inference: the bench assumes env semantics match the RTL elaboration
    byte-for-byte; width sampling, item geometry, reference-model calls and coverage
    thresholds all derive from HammingConf, so a single wrong configuration would
    misapply every oracle and mask could false-pass or false-fail'
  investigation_targets:
  - 'tb/test_top.py: hamming_tb_top() HammingConf.compute() call'
  - 'tb/scoreboard.py: _check_geometry()'
  - 'tb/dut_helper.py: HammingDutPins width sampling defaults'
  recommended_action: Read back the actual elaborated widths (e.g. len(dut.data_in),
