===== IMPROVEMENT DECISION (iteration 1) =====
schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W-ADAPTIVE-SKIP-MASKS-PARAMETER-COVERAGE
  failure_class: stimulus
  failure_mechanism: 'insufficient_parameter_exploration + scenario_not_executed:
    the generated bench pairs an adaptive log-and-skip (sequences.py _targets -> test.py
    elaboration_applies -> pass-without-stimulus) with a Makefile/worker that only
    ever elaborates the RTL default (DATA_WIDTH=4, SECDED=0), so the plan''s SECDED=1
    and non-4-width scenarios report ''1 item checked, 1 passed'' without exercising
    the DUT (corroborated by merged coverage: secded_on/width_1,8,11,16/secded_parity_*
    all 0)'
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: All 10 tests ran under the single default elaboration (DATA_WIDTH=4,
    SECDED=0); TC3/TC5/TC7 and the elaboration-gated corners/randomized configs passed
    via log-and-skip, so the SECDED path (overall-parity bit, ordering shift, even-weight
    property) and the R=2/R=4/R=5 width geometries were never exercised. Merged aggregate
    coverage is 41.67% with zero hits on the SECDED/width bins the plan requires,
    yet every test reports pass because report_phase only enforces zero mismatches
    and, for inapplicable elaborations, skips without the item guard.
  consequence: 'The regression gives false confidence: the freeze contract''s per-configuration
    verification goals are decorative, a DUT defect confined to SECDED behavior or
    to DATA_WIDTH in {1,8,11,16} would pass undetected, and the phantom primed (0,0)
    monitor item further masks the unexercised status by reporting a plausible ''1
    item checked'' for skipped tests.'
candidate_interventions:
- 'tb/Makefile: key DATA_WIDTH/SECDED defaults off UVM_TESTNAME so each test elaborates
  its plan-target configuration (TC1/2/4/6 -> 4,0; TC3/8/corner -> 4,1; TC5 -> 8,0;
  TC7 -> 1,0 or 11,0; randomized -> 8,1), keeping ?= semantics so explicit runner
  overrides still win'
- 'tb/test.py report_phase: change the inapplicable-elaboration branch from silent
  pass to a loud ''UNEXERCISED'' AssertionError (the existing _num_items_checked>0
  guard already covers the applicable case), making silent no-ops impossible once
  each test has a guaranteed target elaboration'
- 'tb/monitor.py: suppress the first primed (data_in=0, code_out=0) sample so skipped
  tests report 0 items (supports the unexercised detection; does not by itself exercise
  the parameter matrix)'
- 'tb/coverage.py + tb/test.py: enforce per-configuration coverage goals in report_phase
  (deferred: high false-failure risk until multi-elaboration runs exist)'
selected_intervention:
  type: 'TB-only regression-scope fix: per-test elaboration selection (Makefile DATA_WIDTH/SECDED
    defaults keyed by UVM_TESTNAME) plus converting the silent log-and-skip path into
    a loud ''unexercised'' failure in HammingTestBase.report_phase'
  expected_effect:
  - 'Each plan scenario now runs on its target (DATA_WIDTH, SECDED): SECDED=1 stimulus
    (TC3, TC8, corner SECDED checks) and non-4 widths (TC5 -> 8, TC7/corner -> 1/11/16)
    exercise real DUT transactions instead of skipping'
  - 'Functional coverage rises toward the plan goals: secded_on, secded_parity_zero/one,
    width_1/8/11/16 and the data_x_secded / width_x_secded cross bins receive hits,
    and the SECDED ordering-shift / even-weight / R-boundary structural checks actually
    execute'
  - Under the applicable-elaboration item guard, every passing test now proves real
    stimulus was scored, so a regression back to the single-default-elaboration runner
    fails loudly as 'unexercised' rather than reporting pass
regression_risks:
- If the external runner ever passes explicit DATA_WIDTH/SECDED equal to the old defaults,
  the Makefile ?= mapping is bypassed and the now-strict report_phase turns TC3/TC5/TC7
  into 'unexercised' failures (intended forcing behavior, but it changes pass/fail
  counts and must be understood as such)
- Intentionally subset runs (e.g., only Hamming(7,4)) now require an explicit configuration;
  the fail-on-skip semantics replace the previous always-green adaptive-skip contract
- Scenarios that the plan defines over 'both SECDED modes' still cover only the active
  mode per single run; full matrix closure still needs multiple elaborations, but
  each test at least exercises its own target configuration
validation:
- Re-run the full 10-test regression through the worker flow (plain `make UVM_TESTNAME=<test>`)
  against the modified Makefile
- Expect 10/10 pass with no 'SKIPPED'/'not applicable' logs for any test, every test
  reporting scoreboard item counts that match its driven vector count, and merged
  hamming_encoder_coverage showing secded_on, width_1/8/11/16, and secded_parity_*
  hits > 0
- Confirm the SECDED structural corner sequences (SECDEDOrderingShift, SECDEDCodewordEvenWeight)
  and R=2/R=4/R=5 geometry assertions execute during the regression instead of log-and-skip
- Confirm zero scoreboard mismatches and no X/Z-after-settle strict-sampler failures
  across all 10 runs

