schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: HW-COVERAGE-NOT-ENFORCED
  failure_class: coverage
  failure_mechanism: 'coverage_metric_not_exported + coverage_not_connected_to_observation
    (interacting): the in-process cross-test merge in tb/coverage.py `_merge_per_test_coverage`
    filters per-test YAMLs with an mtime staleness check (`mtime >= self._run_start_time`),
    which in the sequential multi-process regression discards the 9 per-test files
    written by earlier processes, so the promised regression-level aggregate is never
    computed (''excluded 9 stale per-test file(s)'' / ''aggregate merge from 1 per-test
    file(s)'' in every log) and no persistent union view exists; coverage is reported
    only as last-test-wins exports. The headline single-elaboration gap (HW-SINGLE-ELABORATION)
    is real but runner-gated; iteration 1''s fail-loud/per-test-elaboration fix was
    rejected, so this iteration targets the TB-fixable coverage-accounting half while
    preserving the truthful evidence of the 15/36 (41.67%) elaboration ceiling.'
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: 'Every test log shows ''HammingCoverage merge: excluded 9 stale
    per-test file(s)'' followed by ''aggregate merge from 1 per-test file(s)'': the
    mtime-based freshness filter in coverage.py is wrong for a sequential multi-process
    run layout, so the regression-level union of coverage is never computed or persisted;
    the analyzer/human only sees the last test''s overwritten generic export or per-test
    maxima, and the plan''s coverage goals are neither aggregated nor surfaced next
    to each verdict.'
  consequence: The environment cannot demonstrate or enforce the plan's functional-coverage
    goals (randomized-test pass criterion 'functional coverage goals ... are met'
    is never evaluated anywhere), regression-level coverage is silently under-reported,
    and the accumulation mechanism needed to absorb secded_on / width_8 / width_11
    / width_16 bins once the runner drives the DATA_WIDTH x SECDED matrix does not
    exist, keeping HW-SECDED-WIDTH-GAP and HW-SINGLE-ELABORATION masked in the summary.
candidate_interventions:
- Remove the mtime staleness filter in tb/coverage.py `_merge_per_test_coverage` so
  all per-test YAML files present (RUN_ID-scoped when RUN_ID is set) are merged by
  per-bin max hit count.
- Persist the merged union to a machine-readable aggregate file (hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml,
  cocotb-coverage-style bins:_hits shape) and keep logging the true regression-level
  percentage.
- Surface each test's own coverage state (bins hit / total) next to its verdict in
  report_phase (logging only).
- 'Rejected: make inapplicable tests fail loudly / re-drive per-test elaboration from
  the TB -- directly repeats iteration 1''s rejected intervention with no new evidence
  that the runner applies Makefile/test_top parameter selection.'
- 'Rejected: enforce numeric coverage thresholds as pass/fail -- the plan defines
  no numeric goals, and under the (4,0)-only runner enforcement would convert 3 maskable
  scenarios into failures (the iteration-1 outcome).'
selected_intervention:
  type: 'TB-only coverage-accounting fix in tb/coverage.py: (a) drop the per-process
    mtime freshness filter in `_merge_per_test_coverage` (keep RUN_ID scoping; exclude
    only the generic hamming_encoder_coverage.yml), (b) write the merged per-bin-max
    union to hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml in the same bins:_hits shape the
    per-test exports use, (c) log each test''s coverage (bins hit/total, %) in report_phase
    next to its verdict. No elaboration, Makefile, pass/fail, spec, plan, reference-model,
    CONTRACT.md, or RTL change.'
  expected_effect:
  - 'Merge log becomes truthful: ''aggregate merge from 10 per-test file(s)'' with
    no ''excluded ... stale'' warning, computing the true regression-level union percentage
    (still capped at 15/36 = 41.67% while the runner elaborates only (4,0), but now
    accumulative and honest).'
  - hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml persists the per-bin-max union so the analyzer
    can consume a regression-level view instead of the last test's overwritten generic
    export.
  - Each test verdict is accompanied by its coverage state, surfacing (not enforcing)
    the plan coverage goals exactly as the weakness report's recommended_action requests.
  - When the runner later drives the DATA_WIDTH x SECDED matrix, the repaired merge
    automatically accumulates secded_on / width_8 / width_11 / width_16 and the width_x_secded
    cross bins - the mechanism HW-SECDED-WIDTH-GAP depends on.
  - All 10 tests keep passing with unchanged verdicts (logging-only change; no new
    pass/fail criterion is invented).
regression_risks:
- Merging files from a previous regression if a later run only partially overwrites
  per-test YAMLs; mitigated by preserving RUN_ID scoping and by each test overwriting
  its own stable per-test filename at report_phase.
- The aggregate merge parses per-test YAML from the shared directory; malformed/legacy
  files are already skipped via try/continue, so no new failure path is added.
- Analysis pipelines keyed on the 'excluded N stale' warning string will no longer
  see it - expected evidence of the fix (per-test 0-hit exports for TC3/TC5/TC7 remain
  unchanged, still attesting the elaboration gap).
- No pass/fail, elaboration, or generic-export behavior changes, so no test-verdict
  churn or runner interaction is introduced.
validation:
- Rerun the 10-test regression under the default runner; confirm 10/10 tests still
  pass and each log shows 'aggregate merge from 10 per-test file(s)' (or the RUN_ID-scoped
  count) with no 'excluded ... stale' warning.
- Confirm hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml exists with per-bin maxima (e.g.,
  data_in_cov 5/5, even_weight/odd_weight > 0, secded_on=0 and width_1/8/11/16=0 while
  the runner stays (4,0)) and the logged aggregate percentage equals 41.67% (the true
  union ceiling under single elaboration).
- Confirm per-test exports (including TC3/TC5/TC7 0/36 and HammingRandomizedTest 15/36)
  are unchanged, preserving the evidence chain for the deferred runner-side elaboration
  fix.
- Confirm no changes to test verdicts, scoreboard counts, monitor item counts, or
  coverage sampling counts relative to iteration 2.

