schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W2-SKIPPED-TESTS-PASS
  failure_class: skip_semantics_false_pass
  failure_mechanism: 'false_pass + scenario_not_executed (interacting, runner-gated):
    the adaptive-skip path (HammingTestBase.report_phase -> ''TEST SKIPPED ... passing
    without stimulus'' when elaboration_applies(conf) is false) returns an implicit
    pass, and no machine-readable artifact records which tests skipped, which (DATA_WIDTH,SECDED)
    elaboration each test actually ran, or which plan scenarios executed; the worker
    elaborates every test with the default (4,0) only, so TC3/TC5/TC7 publish 0 transactions
    while the regression still reports 10/10 pass'
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: 'All 10 tests pass under the single default elaboration (DATA_WIDTH=4,
    SECDED=0), but HammingTC3Test (TC3), HammingTC5Test (TC5) and HammingTC7Test (TC7)
    log ''TEST SKIPPED ... passing without stimulus'' with 0 published transactions
    and 0 scoreboard items; the aggregate coverage proves the gap (15/36 = 41.67%:
    secded_on=0, width_1/8/11/16=0, all secded crosses 0), and the scenario analyzer
    records executed_ids=[] because no per-test execution/skip record is emitted;
    iteration 1''s verdict-changing fix (fail on unexercised skip) was rejected with
    3 failures, confirming the safe path is visibility, not verdict changes.'
  consequence: A 10/10 green run hides that 3 of the 8 directed plan scenarios and
    every SECDED / alternate-width plan objective executed zero stimulus; verification
    quality cannot improve because the loop cannot distinguish executed from skipped
    scenarios (scenario_quality=0, executed_ids=[]), and any future regression that
    silently stops driving a scenario will still pass, perpetuating W1/W3.
candidate_interventions:
- 'TB-only execution/skip ledger: in HammingTestBase.report_phase export a per-test
  YAML record {test, data_width, secded, applicable, executed, items_checked/passed/mismatches,
  scenario_id, skip_reason} and merge all per-test records (RUN_ID-scoped, excluding
  generic/aggregate, exactly mirroring tb/coverage.py) into tb/hamming_encoder_execution_aggregate.yml
  with tests_total/tests_executed/tests_skipped and the executed scenario-ID list;
  also emit a WARNING-level ''TEST SKIPPED -> SCENARIO <id> NOT EXECUTED'' line. Verdicts,
  ConfigDB keys, CONTRACT, and interfaces unchanged.'
- 'Makefile per-test elaboration defaults keyed by UVM_TESTNAME (DATA_WIDTH/SECDED
  ?= per test) to actually elaborate TC3 at (4,1) and TC5 at (8,0). Not selected:
  it is the untried half of the rejected iteration-1 experiment family, touches the
  compile/elaboration path, cannot cover TC7''s six configurations or TC4/TC6/TC8''s
  dual-SECDED matrix in one elaboration per simulation, and needs the runner to keep
  invoking per-test; it is the runner-side root fix (W1) and should be driven by the
  regression harness once the ledger makes the residual gaps auditable.'
- 'Enforce coverage closure / fail-on-skip as regression pass criteria (W3 and the
  second half of W2''s recommendation). Deferred: changes verdicts and duplicates
  the rejected iteration-1 approach; it should be owned by the acceptance-criteria/runner
  side after multi-elaboration is possible.'
- 'no_change / re-run evidence only: rejected - it adds no information and leaves
  skips un-auditable.'
selected_intervention:
  type: 'TB-only reporting fix in tb/test.py: per-test execution/skip ledger YAML
    export + RUN_ID-scoped aggregate merge (following the accepted tb/coverage.py
    pattern) + WARNING-level ''TEST SKIPPED -> SCENARIO <id> NOT EXECUTED'' log; no
    change to pass/fail verdicts, no new ConfigDB keys, no contract/spec/plan/model/RTL
    change'
  expected_effect:
  - 'Skips become visible and machine-readable: under the default elaboration the
    aggregate ledger truthfully reports tests_total=10, tests_skipped=3 (TC3/TC5/TC7
    with reasons), tests_executed=7, and lists executed scenario IDs TC1/TC2/TC4/TC6/TC8
    + corner + randomized, closing the executed_ids=[] scenario-quality gap without
    inventing stimulus.'
  - 'Per-configuration auditability (W1 recommendation): every per-test record carries
    the actual (DATA_WIDTH, SECDED) and checked/item counts, so the run''s configuration
    coverage is auditable against hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml (width_4/secded_off
    only) instead of inferred, and zero-execution scenarios correlate exactly with
    the zero coverage bins.'
  - All 10 tests keep their verdicts (logging/export-only, try/except-wrapped), so
    the acceptance criteria are preserved; when the runner later drives the DATA_WIDTH
    x SECDED matrix, the ledger auto-accumulates the newly executed scenarios with
    no further TB change.
  - 'W3 remains surfaced not violated: coverage goals stay report-only, but the analyzer
    now has ground-truth executed-scenario data from the TB itself.'
regression_risks:
- Unguarded file I/O in report_phase could raise and flip a verdict - must be wrapped
  in try/except like tb/coverage.py's export path so failures degrade to a warning.
- Stale per-test ledger files from a previous run could pollute the aggregate when
  RUN_ID is unset - reuse coverage.py's RUN_ID scoping and exclude generic/aggregate
  filenames.
- Elevating the skip message to WARNING could be miscounted by a log parser that treats
  warnings as failures - keep the exact 'TEST SKIPPED' prefix and verify uvm_errors/assertion_failures/scoreboard_mismatches
  stay 0.
- Scenario-ID mapping in the ledger could drift from the manifest - derive it from
  generation_manifest.yaml's test->scenario table (or the test class SCENARIO_ID),
  and note that Corner/Randomized intentionally have no SCENARIO_ID.
validation:
- Run the 10-test regression under the default elaboration; assert all 10 tests still
  pass with unchanged verdicts (uvm_errors=0, scoreboard_mismatches=0, assertion_failures=0).
- 'Inspect tb/hamming_encoder_execution_aggregate.yml: tests_total=10, tests_skipped=3,
  skipped scenario IDs = {TC3, TC5, TC7}, executed IDs = {TC1, TC2, TC4, TC6, TC8,
  corner, randomized}, and each record''s elaboration is (4,0).'
- 'Cross-check ledger vs tb/hamming_encoder_coverage_aggregate.yml: configuration
  (4,0) non-zero bins only; every scenario marked executed has non-zero item counts
  and matching coverage hits; skipped scenarios map to the zero bins (secded_on, width_1/8/11/16,
  secded crosses).'
- Grep logs for the WARNING 'TEST SKIPPED -> SCENARIO' lines for TC3/TC5/TC7 and confirm
  the 'TEST SKIPPED' prefix is preserved for existing log-based parsing; confirm no
  CONTRACT.md/ConfigDB/interface change.

