schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W01
  failure_class: stimulus
  failure_mechanism: 'scenario_not_executed + insufficient_parameter_exploration (interacting,
    runner-gated): the worker invokes make per test with no DATA_WIDTH/SECDED/-G override,
    so every test elaborates the RTL default (DATA_WIDTH=4, SECDED=0); tests whose
    mapped scenario targets another elaboration (TC3->4,1; TC5->8,0; TC7->{1,11,16};
    SECDED and width-gated corners) take the adaptive log-and-skip path in HammingTestBase.report_phase
    and pass with 0 items checked (vacuous pass). This single root cause drives W01
    plus W02 (secded_on and secded_parity_* bins at 0), W03 (width_1/8/11/16 at 0)
    and part of W05 (randomized space collapsed to data_in at (4,0)). Iteration 1
    was rejected solely because it shipped the fail-loud half (test.py/test_top.py)
    without the elaboration mechanism; that mechanism (Makefile per-test defaults)
    was never implemented and is now verifiable with the truthful per-drive items,
    fixed coverage merge, and execution ledger built in iterations 2-4.

    '
  source: mixed
  confidence: medium
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: '10/10 tests pass yet TC3/TC5/TC7 publish 0 transactions (execution
    ledger: 3 skipped, ''inapplicable to (4,0)''); aggregate coverage is 41.67% (15/36)
    with secded_on, secded_parity_zero/one, width_1/8/11/16 and every secded_on cross-cell
    at 0. All checkers, sequences, scoreboard and coverage are HammingConf-parameterized
    (no width-4 hard-coding), so the TB is structurally ready to run the plan''s other
    elaborations; spec section 6 cross-checks (4,1) and (8,0) bit-exactly.

    '
  consequence: 'The SECDED branch (overall-parity bit, bit-order shift, even-weight
    property) and the R=2/R=4/R=5 width geometries are never simulated, so a DUT defect
    confined to those configurations would pass undetected, and the frozen plan''s
    per-configuration verification goals are decorative while every test is green.

    '
candidate_interventions:
- 'tb/Makefile: per-test default elaboration matrix keyed by UVM_TESTNAME (TC1/TC2->(4,0);
  TC3/TC4/TC6/TC8->(4,1); TC5->(8,0); TC7->(1,0); CornerTest->(16,0); RandomizedTest->(8,1)),
  applied only when the caller passes no explicit DATA_WIDTH/SECDED override; no verdict-logic
  change'
- 'tb/test.py: convert the inapplicable-elaboration branch from pass to a loud ''UNEXERCISED''
  AssertionError (iteration 1''s remaining half; rejected previously without the matrix,
  still changes pass/fail counts and is therefore out of scope for this safe iteration)'
- 'tb/coverage.py: add a verdict-changing coverage gate on the plan bins (deferred:
  would fail the current single-elaboration acceptance run exactly like iteration
  1; belongs to a runner-driven matrix)'
- 'no_change/defer: accept that the gap is purely runner-gated and the TB cannot exercise
  more than one elaboration per simulation'
selected_intervention:
  type: 'TB-only, smallest effective change: add a UVM_TESTNAME-keyed default elaboration
    matrix to tb/Makefile (per-test DATA_WIDTH/SECDED defaults applied when the caller
    provides no explicit override, so the observed override-free make invocations
    now elaborate each scenario''s target configuration), combined with no change
    to any pass/fail logic. No RTL, spec, plan, reference-model, CONTRACT.md, generation_manifest
    or test.py behavior change.

    '
  expected_effect:
  - 'W01 closed: TC3/TC5/TC7 become applicable, drive their real scenario vectors,
    and the execution ledger reports tests_executed=10, skipped=0 instead of 3 vacuous
    passes'
  - 'W02 closed: SECDED=1 elaborations (TC3/TC4/TC6/TC8 at (4,1), Randomized at (8,1))
    hit secded_on, secded_parity_zero/one, the data_x_secded secded_on cross-cells,
    and the secded_overall_even_parity assertion plus SECDED corner sequences actually
    execute'
  - 'W03 reduced: width_cov width_1/8/16 and the width_x_secded cells (4,1)/(8,0)/(8,1)/(1,0)/(16,0)
    receive hits via TC7->(1,0), TC5->(8,0), CornerTest->(16,0) (running parity_bit_count_transition
    at R=5); aggregate coverage rises from 41.67% toward ~86% (31/36, residual gaps:
    width_11 and secded_on x width 1/16)'
  - 'W05 reduced: the randomized stream moves to the plan constraint cell (data_width=8,
    secded=1), exercising wider XOR trees under SECDED with all 1000 vectors still
    bit-exact scored'
  - All 10 tests keep passing with unchanged checker/scoreboard semantics (same assertions,
    wider elaboration reach); spec-section-6-verified (4,1)/(8,0) configurations carry
    the minimum DUT-conformance risk
regression_risks:
- If the DUT deviates from the reference model at a newly exercised elaboration (principally
  (1,0), (16,0), (8,1), which lack spec-section-6 cross-checks), the affected test
  now fails - a genuine finding, but one the current acceptance gate would mark as
  a rejected iteration; mitigated by the plan's bit-exact expectations and the parametric
  RTL's verified (4,0)/(4,1)/(8,0) conformance
- If the runner passes DATA_WIDTH/SECDED explicitly or via exported environment defaults
